.\" $GergiOS: bluetooth.3,v 1.0 2026/07/10 $
.\"
.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt BLUETOOTH 3
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm libbluetooth
.Nd Bluetooth daemon client library
.Sh LIBRARY
.lb libbluetooth
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In bluetooth.h
.Ft bt_handle_t *
.Fn bt_open void
.Ft void
.Fn bt_close "bt_handle_t *handle"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_start_discovery "bt_handle_t *handle"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_stop_discovery "bt_handle_t *handle"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_get_devices "bt_handle_t *handle" "bt_device_t *devices" "int max"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_connect "bt_handle_t *handle" "const bt_bdaddr_t *bdaddr"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_disconnect "bt_handle_t *handle" "uint16_t conn_handle" "uint8_t reason"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_get_connections "bt_handle_t *handle" "bt_connection_t *conns" "int max"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_set_name "bt_handle_t *handle" "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_set_discoverable "bt_handle_t *handle" "int enable"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_set_connectable "bt_handle_t *handle" "int enable"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_get_status "bt_handle_t *handle" "bt_status_t *status"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_pair "bt_handle_t *handle" "const bt_bdaddr_t *bdaddr"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_unpair "bt_handle_t *handle" "const bt_bdaddr_t *bdaddr"
.Ft int
.Fn bt_bdaddr_parse "const char *str" "bt_bdaddr_t *bdaddr"
.Ft char *
.Fn bt_bdaddr_format "const bt_bdaddr_t *bdaddr" "char *buf" "size_t bufsize"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library provides a C API for communicating with the Bluetooth daemon
.Pq bluetoothd
on GergiOS.
.Pp
The library communicates with the daemon via MINIX IPC:
it looks up the daemon endpoint in the Data Store and sends
command messages using
.Xr sendrec 2 .
.Pp
All functions return
.Dv BT_OK
(0) on success, or a negative errno on failure.
.Sh INITIALIZATION
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_open
Opens a connection to the Bluetooth daemon.
Returns a handle, or
.Dv NULL
on error with
.Va errno
set.
.It Fn bt_close
Closes the connection and frees the handle.
.El
.Sh DEVICE DISCOVERY
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_start_discovery
Starts an inquiry scan for nearby Bluetooth devices.
.It Fn bt_stop_discovery
Stops the ongoing inquiry scan.
.It Fn bt_get_devices
Retrieves the list of discovered devices.
The
.Fa devices
array must have room for at least
.Fa max
elements.
Returns the number of devices written, or a negative errno.
.El
.Sh CONNECTION MANAGEMENT
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_connect
Initiates a connection to the remote device at the given BD_ADDR.
.It Fn bt_disconnect
Disconnects from the remote device identified by the HCI connection handle.
The
.Fa reason
is an HCI status code (default 0x13 = Remote User Terminated).
.It Fn bt_get_connections
Retrieves the list of active connections.
.El
.Sh LOCAL CONFIGURATION
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_set_name
Sets the local Bluetooth device name.
.It Fn bt_set_discoverable
Enables or disables inquiry scan (discoverability).
.It Fn bt_set_connectable
Enables or disables page scan (connectability).
.El
.Sh STATUS AND PAIRING
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_get_status
Returns the daemon status: running flag, device count, connection count.
.It Fn bt_pair
Initiates pairing with a remote device.
.It Fn bt_unpair
Removes pairing with a remote device.
.El
.Sh UTILITY
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn bt_bdaddr_parse
Parses a BD_ADDR string in the format
.Dq XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
into a
.Ft bt_bdaddr_t .
.It Fn bt_bdaddr_format
Formats a
.Ft bt_bdaddr_t
as a colon-separated hexadecimal string.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bt-tool 8 ,
.Xr bluetoothd 8 ,
.Xr sendrec 2
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
library appeared in GergiOS Phase 8.6.
